I have started to move my Japanese stuff from a SunOS 4.1.3
machine to a DEC Alpha OSF/1 V3.2 machine. The first
step is kterm. I built kterm-6.1.0 with almost no complaints
(had to comment out something about X_GETTIMEOFDAY in misc.c
to get it to link). 

To test it I ftp'd a Japanese file from the Sun machine over to the
Alpha. Then I tried viewing it with the new kterm. No go, just garbage.
BUT, if I telnet over to the Sun from the SAME kterm window, and
view the copy of the file over there, it looks fine. If I look at
the file with emacs, I can see that it did ftp over correctly, with
the funny codes intact (I tried euc and new-jis versions).

Anyone have any idea why kterm works when viewing a file remotely
but not locally? Is this a 32 versus 64 issue? Is there other
settings in stty or app-defaults I need to change?

Thanks for any suggestions,

Joel
schulman@hrl.com
 



