Kapsch <nacl@serviceteam.co.uk> writes:

> 
> how the hell do you stop the banner page from printing under Dec Unix
> 3.2c??????
> 
  It depends on what printer you are using, and how you print from the
  Unix box.

  Try the -h flag to lpr if you are using that command to print.  Check
  out the man page for lpr.

  If you are printing to a local printer on your Unix box, try adding an
  sh entry in your /etc/printcap entry for the printer.  Check out the
  man page for printcap.

  If you are printing to a remote printer, that printer may be local on
  some other workstation.  Change the printcap entry on the appropriate
  machine, as above.

  Read the printer's documentation for info on turning off the burst
  page.  Some printers (e.g. HPs with Jetdirect cards) are configured as
  remote printers from all machines, so you need to use the software
  provided, or configure the printer appropriately from the control
  panel or network connection, or use the lpr -h approach described
  above.

  Good luck,
		Phil
