Jean,

1)  You probably don't need to worry about specifying the BPI and size
of the tape.  I have a tlz07 drive myself and never have.  The only
side effect that I have seen is that dump/rdump report wildly
erroneous  requirements for number of tapes, etc.  Other than that,
the dump runs fine.

2) Mount your iso9660 cdrom with:

mount -t cdfs -o ro -o noversion /dev/[your-cd-dev-here]  /[directory]

Hope this helps

Scott





