> 
> 
> 2) Mount your iso9660 cdrom with:
> 
> mount -t cdfs -o ro -o noversion /dev/[your-cd-dev-here]  /[directory]
> 
> Hope this helps
> 
> Scott

-- 


actually, for #2, try the rrip option first-- it is for the Rock Ridge
Extensions to CDFS, and does nothing if the CD wasn't formatted
with the extensions.  A "noversion" option is normal
for MS-DOS CD applications.

The hierarchy to try is

# mount -t cdfs -o rrip  /dev/your-cd-dev /your-mount-dir
    
    ## for CDs marked as ISO/9660 with Rock Ridge Extensions
	   (the DU V4.0 Freeware CD set is of this type)

   else  use

# mount -t cdfs -o noversion  /dev/your-cd-device /your-mount-dir

 
